WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.520
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.790 --> 00:02.620
Wait!

3
00:03.820 --> 00:05.800
No one else is here except me.

4
00:14.820 --> 00:17.690
[last log]

5
00:17.690 --> 00:19.850
Where's the girl?

6
00:31.730 --> 00:33.500
Freeze.

7
00:51.520 --> 00:53.470
What are you doing?

8
00:53.470 --> 00:56.770
Stay here. Don't go seeking out danger!

9
01:18.030 --> 01:19.620
Shiharu!

10
01:22.150 --> 01:23.960
Shiharu?

11
01:27.560 --> 01:29.100
Yui...

12
01:32.060 --> 01:33.840
Where's Shiharu?

13
01:44.070 --> 01:45.760
Shiharu...

14
01:47.810 --> 01:49.950
S-Shiharu?

15
01:52.980 --> 01:54.670
Shiharu...

16
01:55.660 --> 01:57.120
Why?

17
02:05.350 --> 02:10.370
The girl who was with the Professor...

18
02:15.580 --> 02:17.380
I...

19
02:18.650 --> 02:21.080
I had already met you.

20
02:23.900 --> 02:25.790
Shii...

21
02:27.110 --> 02:30.160
wanted to see these hydrangeas again.

22
02:30.980 --> 02:33.430
That's why I thought maybe, just maybe,

23
02:33.430 --> 02:38.420
I'd find her here.

24
02:42.150 --> 02:46.120
I caught her when she was being carried inside.

25
02:47.650 --> 02:51.950
I called Kyoichi about it, and he asked me to stay with her.

26
02:52.650 --> 02:54.290
I see.

27
02:56.210 --> 02:58.620
Then the person I saw at my thesis presentation...

28
02:58.620 --> 03:01.520
Shii's body was already weak by that time.

29
03:01.520 --> 03:05.600
She wasn't supposed to leave the house.

30
03:05.600 --> 03:11.520
But she insisted on going.

31
03:13.610 --> 03:15.200
Shii.

32
03:15.200 --> 03:16.650
Are you okay?

33
03:16.650 --> 03:18.290
Yeah.

34
03:18.290 --> 03:20.080
You saw enough?

35
03:22.530 --> 03:24.410
Yes, thank you.

36
03:32.060 --> 03:33.960
I'm sorry.

37
03:34.690 --> 03:38.350
I was so worried my choice

38
03:38.350 --> 03:41.660
had caused you to suffer.

39
03:42.810 --> 03:44.610
Seeing Shiharu there...

40
03:46.520 --> 03:49.500
was the reason I managed to come this far.

41
03:52.730 --> 03:54.830
It's how I managed to find her.

42
03:58.690 --> 04:00.250
I...

43
04:01.250 --> 04:03.800
I caused my father great anguish as well.

44
04:06.900 --> 04:08.410
Welcome home.

45
04:09.250 --> 04:10.990
Could we talk?

46
04:11.900 --> 04:13.240
Sure.

47
04:16.310 --> 04:21.330
You didn't take Shiharu out today, did you?

48
04:22.440 --> 04:26.810
Haruka was acting strange during his presentation today.

49
04:26.810 --> 04:28.660
We didn't go out.

50
04:29.770 --> 04:32.370
Shiharu was home all day?

51
04:33.730 --> 04:35.660
Really?

52
04:37.270 --> 04:38.700
Yeah.

53
04:42.770 --> 04:44.410
Okay.

54
04:45.690 --> 04:49.730
My father noticed. He knew the truth.

55
04:51.050 --> 04:57.050
Shii's health only got worse after that day.

56
04:59.600 --> 05:02.560
My father insisted he'd hire a helper for her,

57
05:02.560 --> 05:07.780
and wanted me to go live a "normal" life.

58
05:07.780 --> 05:09.710
What?

59
05:10.600 --> 05:12.750
How could you say that?

60
05:14.020 --> 05:16.580
It's for Shiharu's sake as well.

61
05:18.310 --> 05:22.330
She won't ever get better again?

62
05:28.060 --> 05:31.830
I've always thought something was up.

63
05:31.830 --> 05:34.550
But now I'm certain.

64
05:39.380 --> 05:42.750
This doesn't have anything to do with your research, does it?

65
05:43.980 --> 05:45.410
Dad.

66
05:50.020 --> 05:52.290
I believe I'm responsible.

67
05:55.190 --> 05:57.210
What did you do?

68
05:57.730 --> 06:00.250
Dad, please. Why?

69
06:00.250 --> 06:03.160
I'll tell you everything soon enough.

70
06:05.190 --> 06:08.830
Just give me a bit more time.

71
06:11.530 --> 06:16.360
I want to keep Shiharu a secret for now.

72
06:16.360 --> 06:19.740
Once it's all said and done, I'll explain.

73
06:19.740 --> 06:22.040
I just don't understand.

74
06:22.040 --> 06:24.800
You're not making any sense!

75
06:32.280 --> 06:34.040
Shii.

76
06:36.160 --> 06:38.580
Everything will be okay, I promise.

77
06:40.690 --> 06:43.010
We're always going to be together, okay?

78
07:03.750 --> 07:05.760
Thank you.

79
07:09.080 --> 07:11.580
But I'm fine now.

80
07:17.000 --> 07:19.080
What do you mean?

81
07:24.270 --> 07:26.750
Mari.

82
07:31.190 --> 07:34.470
I want you to go live your own life.

83
07:41.060 --> 07:42.620
You mean...

84
07:44.630 --> 07:47.390
I can't stay?

85
07:58.770 --> 08:03.170
You don't want me to stay?

86
08:08.870 --> 08:10.250
Yeah.

87
08:14.910 --> 08:17.050
Why?

88
08:19.420 --> 08:21.220
Why?

89
08:30.880 --> 08:32.750
Don't cry.

90
08:37.910 --> 08:39.620
No.

91
08:42.580 --> 08:44.200
No!

92
08:46.380 --> 08:51.700
All this time, I had been searching for Shii.

93
08:52.500 --> 08:55.790
But I was searching for my father's truth, too.

94
09:00.770 --> 09:03.620
So I was the only one who knew nothing.

95
09:06.120 --> 09:09.010
Shii didn't want you to know.

96
09:10.670 --> 09:13.470
She wanted to pretend she never existed.

97
09:16.270 --> 09:18.010
Shii.

98
09:19.150 --> 09:25.170
You wanted him to remember you at your best, didn't you?

99
09:30.440 --> 09:35.710
Then you wouldn't love me if I became bald, ugly, and dumb.

100
09:35.710 --> 09:38.480
Well, that wouldn't be you anymore, would it?

101
09:38.480 --> 09:41.970
Yeah. I think so, too.

102
09:49.310 --> 09:51.700
I wasn't able to understand.

103
09:53.150 --> 09:54.790
I knew nothing.

104
09:58.690 --> 10:00.350
Shiharu.

105
10:00.900 --> 10:02.570
I'm sorry.

106
10:12.200 --> 10:14.000
I'm so sorry.

107
10:49.200 --> 10:54.060
Isn't it your duty to ensure

108
10:54.060 --> 10:56.000
the secret never gets out?

109
10:56.850 --> 11:00.160
Why would you kill her?

110
11:01.710 --> 11:03.620
Is it jealousy?

111
11:05.020 --> 11:09.710
Are you jealous of the Mataji?

112
13:09.210 --> 13:10.750
Shiharu.

113
13:18.270 --> 13:19.450
We have to get her out.

114
13:19.450 --> 13:21.060
Right.

115
13:21.060 --> 13:23.160
Don't touch her.

116
13:26.400 --> 13:29.000
Don't touch that woman.

117
13:32.300 --> 13:34.240
She's about to break.

118
13:35.330 --> 13:38.160
- Shii! - What are you going to do to her?

119
13:39.730 --> 13:41.910
I'll make it so she never existed.

120
13:45.730 --> 13:47.800
I'll eliminate her myself.

121
13:49.730 --> 13:51.750
Shiharu exists.

122
13:54.210 --> 13:56.230
Why do you think that?

123
14:09.440 --> 14:12.150
How is my blood any different than yours?

124
14:14.810 --> 14:16.790
Why would you do something like this?

125
14:18.400 --> 14:21.580
Because everything is preordained.

126
14:22.620 --> 14:24.750
What makes a person?

127
14:25.350 --> 14:28.870
Their "birth" or "upbringing"?

128
14:31.650 --> 14:33.450
The answer, is their birth.

129
14:36.150 --> 14:39.930
Genes determine the fate of every individual.

130
14:42.740 --> 14:44.320
No.

131
14:46.150 --> 14:48.270
Humans must defy their given fate!

132
14:48.270 --> 14:50.580
I am not human!

133
15:01.240 --> 15:07.590
Who am I? Who? Who am I!

134
15:08.350 --> 15:10.860
Who am I?

135
15:10.860 --> 15:12.870
That woman is no human either.

136
15:12.870 --> 15:15.000
She is human!

137
15:17.230 --> 15:21.290
You and Shiharu are both human beings!

138
15:21.290 --> 15:23.470
Quiet!

139
15:31.690 --> 15:33.250
Have to fight...

140
15:34.820 --> 15:36.990
The monster...

141
15:48.450 --> 15:50.450
Shii, no!

142
16:01.330 --> 16:03.120
Enough.

143
16:04.240 --> 16:05.970
Don't overexert yourself.

144
16:06.790 --> 16:08.960
You're another failure.

145
16:19.550 --> 16:21.460
Stop this!

146
16:22.280 --> 16:24.110
Stop!

147
16:33.650 --> 16:35.380
Stand back!

148
16:46.780 --> 16:48.550
Run! Hurry!

149
16:50.540 --> 16:55.790
Mataji!

150
17:07.180 --> 17:09.250
- Are you okay? - Shii!

151
17:15.290 --> 17:17.820
- Get her in at once! - Yes, ma'am.

152
17:17.820 --> 17:19.950
Stay back!

153
17:19.950 --> 17:21.370
Don't touch her!

154
17:21.370 --> 17:24.230
She will be cared for at our facility.

155
17:24.230 --> 17:27.700
- She needs medical attention! - Shiharu is not your "Holy Woman"!

156
17:34.560 --> 17:36.300
Shiharu?

157
17:36.300 --> 17:38.250
It's fine.

158
17:39.920 --> 17:42.290
I called them here.

159
18:42.690 --> 18:46.480
Why was I born?

160
18:53.830 --> 18:55.750
Why...

161
18:57.310 --> 19:00.450
Why have you people created life?

162
19:04.440 --> 19:07.250
Why was I given life?

163
19:11.520 --> 19:13.870
Why was I brought into this world?

164
19:18.590 --> 19:20.540
Why?

165
19:25.580 --> 19:27.220
Why?

166
19:59.190 --> 20:00.970
Don't touch that.

167
20:09.270 --> 20:11.000
Hand it over.

168
20:14.870 --> 20:17.800
If I pull this trigger, will it shoot?

169
20:22.270 --> 20:25.330
Take me to where they are.

170
20:39.270 --> 20:43.750
She'll be okay, won't she?

171
20:43.750 --> 20:46.200
We've done all that we can for her.

172
20:46.740 --> 20:48.840
Will she recover?

173
20:50.040 --> 20:51.570
Doctor, please!

174
20:51.570 --> 20:55.210
You can't!

175
21:00.900 --> 21:04.000
Keeping me out of the loop, again?

176
21:05.650 --> 21:08.520
- Dr. Senba, please. - Quiet!

177
21:08.520 --> 21:11.250
- Ms. Kasuga. - I'm fine.

178
21:12.120 --> 21:14.120
Get everyone outside.

179
21:22.940 --> 21:27.910
You people...

180
21:28.480 --> 21:31.120
You took my precious grandson away from me.

181
21:32.600 --> 21:34.270
I will kill that clone

182
21:34.270 --> 21:37.540
and every last one of you!

183
21:54.150 --> 21:55.960
I'm sorry.

184
22:07.020 --> 22:10.790
You think I would forgive you?

185
22:33.480 --> 22:36.230
I cannot forgive you either.

186
22:36.230 --> 22:37.980
What?

187
22:37.980 --> 22:40.980
Your own child is in there, dying.

188
22:40.980 --> 22:43.040
So what are you doing?

189
22:45.440 --> 22:49.990
You call me a mother, yet I was never informed of her birth.

190
22:49.990 --> 22:53.770
I cannot forgive any of you!

191
22:53.770 --> 22:55.970
Fine, then don't forgive.

192
23:01.150 --> 23:02.960
Just please...

193
23:04.770 --> 23:06.720
Please save Shiharu.

194
23:07.570 --> 23:09.040
What are you doing?

195
23:09.040 --> 23:11.760
You brought Shiharu into this world.

196
23:11.760 --> 23:14.540
You're the only one who can save her.

197
23:21.810 --> 23:23.960
Please, save her.

198
23:24.770 --> 23:29.160
Will you leave your own creation to die on her own?

199
23:34.850 --> 23:37.160
Let her live.

200
23:38.990 --> 23:42.150
I will do anything, so please.

201
23:42.150 --> 23:45.120
- Don't take her from us! - Enough!

202
23:48.880 --> 23:51.040
If you want to kill me, go ahead.

203
23:53.060 --> 23:55.420
I only ask that you save her.

204
24:11.490 --> 24:16.830
Why couldn't Shii be born the way other kids were,

205
24:17.650 --> 24:19.730
and live like any other girl?

206
24:19.730 --> 24:21.840
Stop.

207
24:24.440 --> 24:29.500
Do you understand how it feels?

208
24:31.060 --> 24:34.120
To want to disappear from your loved ones?

209
24:35.750 --> 24:38.880
- What? - For the sake of her beloved,

210
24:39.980 --> 24:43.370
she would pretend like she never existed.

211
24:46.940 --> 24:49.750
That was her wish from the start.

212
24:52.920 --> 24:57.790
But no one can simply "not exist".

213
25:00.480 --> 25:05.260
When I reunited with her,

214
25:06.560 --> 25:08.450
I finally understood.

215
25:10.060 --> 25:15.830
She is the reason I learned to feel again.

216
25:17.590 --> 25:22.350
You brought a wonderful human being into this world.

217
26:05.630 --> 26:08.000
My daughter...

218
26:28.980 --> 26:32.750
Will she be okay?

219
26:32.750 --> 26:35.170
I am no doctor.

220
26:36.190 --> 26:37.920
Sorry.

221
26:38.570 --> 26:44.560
Simply put, the damage done to her DNA is beyond medical repair.

222
26:44.560 --> 26:46.040
However...

223
26:47.400 --> 26:50.840
I created her. I can save her as well.

224
26:52.840 --> 26:54.910
Really?

225
26:58.020 --> 27:01.000
I won't abandon her anymore.

226
27:03.020 --> 27:05.000
You're sure about this?

227
27:07.270 --> 27:09.120
It's the reason...

228
27:12.020 --> 27:14.750
I was given life.

229
27:18.150 --> 27:20.100
Go home.

230
27:20.100 --> 27:21.970
You'll disturb me.

231
27:43.270 --> 27:46.050
Could I have a moment?

232
27:53.310 --> 27:58.690
We will care for our Mataji here.

233
27:58.690 --> 28:01.060
"Mataji"?

234
28:01.060 --> 28:03.480
Our Holy Woman.

235
28:03.480 --> 28:09.120
I was told you knew that is why she was created?

236
28:11.540 --> 28:15.730
She was always meant to live alongside our people.

237
28:15.730 --> 28:17.820
Do you understand?

238
28:17.820 --> 28:22.660
She will adopt a new identity.

239
28:23.520 --> 28:25.460
Shii...

240
28:27.520 --> 28:31.560
Will she live a normal life here?

241
28:31.560 --> 28:33.480
Not to worry.

242
28:33.480 --> 28:36.480
We will provide everything our Mataji needs.

243
28:36.480 --> 28:40.000
She will live comfortably here.

244
28:40.490 --> 28:46.000
Please understand this is what she desires as well.

245
29:22.350 --> 29:24.420
You weren't able to see her again?

246
29:29.910 --> 29:33.350
Everything you said was true.

247
29:33.350 --> 29:35.450
I'm surprised you're still sane.

248
29:39.530 --> 29:42.630
You were fighting a lonely fight.

249
29:43.980 --> 29:46.010
I wasn't fighting alone.

250
29:46.830 --> 29:50.070
I had help from plenty of others.

251
29:50.070 --> 29:51.960
Yourself included.

252
29:54.700 --> 29:58.170
I had the wrong idea about you.

253
30:00.990 --> 30:06.750
I thought people needed allies to survive.

254
30:08.270 --> 30:11.410
You're acting like I have no one taking my side.

255
30:14.350 --> 30:18.670
I decided to take a page out of your notebook.

256
30:19.770 --> 30:23.950
I'm done obeying orders.

257
30:26.520 --> 30:30.410
What about you? Got any plans now that it's over?

258
30:32.330 --> 30:34.120
I don't know.

259
30:39.320 --> 30:41.540
Good afternoon, sir.

260
30:41.540 --> 30:42.970
See you around.

261
30:48.600 --> 30:50.070
I've brought the money for the hospital director.

262
30:50.070 --> 30:52.350
Can you hand it to them?

263
30:52.350 --> 30:54.310
- Of course. - Thank you.

264
30:55.520 --> 30:57.810
Have you finished tying your loose ends?

265
30:57.810 --> 31:00.870
Yeah. Just about.

266
31:01.490 --> 31:04.620
Do you still stand by your convictions?

267
31:06.440 --> 31:08.620
I wonder.

268
31:09.150 --> 31:11.470
What was the right choice to make?

269
31:13.310 --> 31:18.440
The person you wanted to protect is here, isn't she?

270
31:18.440 --> 31:20.140
Yes.

271
31:20.980 --> 31:23.980
I'm sorry I never told you.

272
31:23.980 --> 31:25.380
It's fine.

273
31:26.200 --> 31:31.580
By protecting her, you were protecting him as well.

274
31:33.370 --> 31:35.920
That's the excuse I tell myself.

275
31:41.650 --> 31:47.590
All in favor of dismissing President Nanase.

276
32:07.350 --> 32:09.080
I understand.

277
32:17.570 --> 32:20.960
You have stood by your convictions.

278
32:31.940 --> 32:34.010
I'm sorry, sir.

279
32:38.020 --> 32:39.790
No, this is fine.

280
32:54.900 --> 33:01.550
We shall now commence the recognition of our new Mataji.

281
33:05.350 --> 33:10.830
I will open with some words from our Holy Woman, the Mataji.

282
33:17.670 --> 33:23.700
"During their lives, humans learn a great many things."

283
33:24.230 --> 33:26.480
"A person's standing, their way of thought,

284
33:26.480 --> 33:30.060
their complications and relationships."

285
33:30.060 --> 33:35.680
"They may learn to prioritize any number of these."

286
33:36.320 --> 33:38.750
"But in truth..."

287
33:39.670 --> 33:41.710
But in truth,

288
33:42.850 --> 33:48.390
there are far more important things to prioritize.

289
33:49.520 --> 33:51.860
The light on one's skin.

290
33:51.860 --> 33:53.960
The wind in one's hair.

291
33:55.110 --> 34:00.960
The moments you share with those you relate to.

292
34:01.660 --> 34:05.000
The exploration of the unknown.

293
34:05.950 --> 34:08.580
The sharing of each other's sorrow.

294
34:09.770 --> 34:11.840
The trust you have in another.

295
34:13.810 --> 34:16.790
The every day.

296
34:18.520 --> 34:21.480
The mundane conversations.

297
34:21.480 --> 34:23.460
The ordinary.

298
34:27.480 --> 34:30.660
The time spent, doing nothing.

299
34:32.060 --> 34:34.630
Aren't these all far more important to life?

300
34:37.020 --> 34:43.250
Those who live think existence itself gives their life meaning.

301
34:44.940 --> 34:47.580
No matter what sort of upbringing they experience.

302
34:50.210 --> 34:52.200
No matter what sort of appearance they may take.

303
34:59.870 --> 35:03.290
That is what I've learned from those around me.

304
35:07.230 --> 35:09.000
So...

305
35:11.310 --> 35:14.200
I live my life now,

306
35:15.270 --> 35:17.460
thinking of those people who taught me well.

307
35:22.850 --> 35:25.170
No matter what I may look like.

308
35:26.230 --> 35:28.540
No matter who I am.

309
35:31.270 --> 35:34.040
I wish to cherish every day I live.

310
35:37.440 --> 35:39.170
To you...

311
35:41.230 --> 35:44.000
To the people beside you...

312
36:08.180 --> 36:11.160
To the people who stayed beside me...

313
36:21.500 --> 36:23.160
Thank you.

314
37:07.140 --> 37:09.310
You're really moving back here?

315
37:09.310 --> 37:10.840
Yeah.

316
37:10.840 --> 37:13.020
I wanted some time to think alone.

317
37:13.020 --> 37:15.040
I see.

318
37:23.060 --> 37:28.380
Your mother didn't give birth to Shiharu solely because of her faith.

319
37:29.940 --> 37:32.210
She was thinking of you as well.

320
37:32.830 --> 37:34.660
What brought this on?

321
37:35.900 --> 37:42.000
Your mother thought her faith is what strained your relationship with her.

322
37:43.690 --> 37:46.000
She believed your sister

323
37:46.900 --> 37:50.050
would ultimately save you.

324
37:51.610 --> 37:53.630
Myself, as well.

325
37:56.230 --> 38:00.840
It was difficult to live together, while keeping Shiharu hidden away.

326
38:05.900 --> 38:07.950
But...

327
38:09.520 --> 38:11.500
I have no regrets.

328
38:12.870 --> 38:16.830
That's the excuse you tell yourself.

329
38:19.890 --> 38:21.460
You're right.

330
38:23.760 --> 38:25.570
I'm kidding.

331
38:25.570 --> 38:27.590
I get it, okay?

332
38:28.690 --> 38:30.080
Yeah.

333
38:33.400 --> 38:35.220
I'll head out soon.

334
38:36.860 --> 38:39.020
You should eat something before you go.

335
38:39.020 --> 38:40.620
I'll whip something up for us.

336
38:43.640 --> 38:45.080
Sounds good.

337
38:45.080 --> 38:48.720
How does okonomiyaki sound? Fishcake included.

338
38:50.480 --> 38:52.850
Your mother always added that, didn't she?

339
38:52.850 --> 38:56.200
I never understood why.

340
39:05.020 --> 39:08.990
Afterwards, my father turned himself in.

341
39:09.520 --> 39:14.270
He confessed how he used company money

342
39:14.270 --> 39:16.750
to cover up the truth of his monetary mismanagement.

343
39:16.750 --> 39:20.160
And you're the one behind all this?

344
39:20.750 --> 39:22.370
That's right.

345
39:22.370 --> 39:25.760
It was all my doing.

346
39:26.810 --> 39:29.690
The cloning tech was kept under wraps

347
39:29.690 --> 39:34.890
with the help of Plantae supporters in the police.

348
39:34.890 --> 39:37.630
The article about it never saw the light of day.

349
39:38.270 --> 39:40.690
[Nichie Pharmaceutical President Arrested for Embezzlement]

350
39:40.690 --> 39:42.210
Yo.

351
39:42.910 --> 39:44.300
Hirama.

352
39:44.300 --> 39:46.350
I'll have the usual.

353
39:46.350 --> 39:48.920
You haven't returned to the lab?

354
39:48.920 --> 39:51.130
No. I've been working part time.

355
39:51.130 --> 39:54.100
Seriously? That's all you've been doing?

356
39:54.100 --> 39:57.540
I wanted to try something new.

357
39:58.560 --> 40:00.450
I get it.

358
40:03.230 --> 40:05.580
I was just reading this article.

359
40:08.940 --> 40:13.080
Sorry I had to be scathing towards your father.

360
40:13.080 --> 40:17.010
It's fine. He wanted the criticism.

361
40:21.020 --> 40:23.120
I owe you, Hirama.

362
40:23.120 --> 40:25.840
Nah, don't say that.

363
40:25.840 --> 40:29.520
I'm more surprised we're both still kicking.

364
40:29.520 --> 40:31.510
You could say that again.

365
40:36.600 --> 40:41.210
A few days after Shiharu was admitted, Keita was found, alive.

366
40:43.770 --> 40:49.180
According to him, Tomoe protected him until the very end.

367
40:49.790 --> 40:52.040
Keita was unharmed.

368
40:54.020 --> 40:59.350
Perhaps Ushio saw himself in Keita, who suffered a genetic disorder.

369
40:59.350 --> 41:01.800
But we will never know the truth.

370
41:03.500 --> 41:07.600
The murders Ushio committed were filed as a case

371
41:07.600 --> 41:10.520
where the culprit was found dead.

372
41:10.520 --> 41:12.950
Nothing more about it was looked into.

373
42:34.020 --> 42:35.710
I won't ever forget.

374
42:35.710 --> 42:37.420
I won't ever forget.

375
43:01.400 --> 43:03.410
Haruka!

376
43:11.990 --> 43:13.850
I haven't been here in so long.

377
43:13.850 --> 43:16.840
Same. I haven't visited since that day.

378
43:20.400 --> 43:22.750
A hydrangea blooming out of season.

379
43:24.820 --> 43:26.620
Let's plant ours here.

380
43:27.250 --> 43:28.750
Okay.

381
43:37.390 --> 43:39.570
Will another one sprout from here?

382
43:39.570 --> 43:41.080
Yeah.

383
43:41.900 --> 43:44.170
I can't wait.

384
43:45.700 --> 43:48.730
Waiting isn't so bad, you know?

385
43:50.780 --> 43:52.400
You're right.

386
43:52.400 --> 43:53.970
Should we get going?

387
43:56.690 --> 43:58.980
Let's come again when they're in bloom.

388
43:58.980 --> 44:00.800
Yeah.

389
44:00.800 --> 44:03.230
I need to find a job before then.

390
44:03.230 --> 44:05.720
How about you return to the lab?

391
44:06.690 --> 44:08.410
Maybe I will.
